---
machine:
  type: controlplane
  nodeLabels:
    topology.kubernetes.io/zone: dmf-u
  install:
    diskSelector:
      model: Samsung SSD 870
    # 2026-07-25: RTX 3090 arrived, tested in the AOOSTAR AG02 dock (ASMedia ASM2464
    # bridge) - never stable, hardware-level flakiness on that dock's bridge chip.
    # 2026-07-28: swapped to a PELADN Link S-3 dock (Intel Barlow Ridge JHL9480 TB5
    # controller) - link itself rock solid, zero disconnects. But the eGPU schematic's
    # NVIDIA extensions (nvidia-open-gpu-kernel-modules-production,
    # nvidia-container-toolkit-production) are fundamentally incompatible with a
    # Thunderbolt-hotplugged GPU on this Talos version: `ext-nvidia-persistenced`
    # blocks boot on /sys/bus/pci/drivers/nvidia existing, which only appears after a
    # successful nvidia.ko load, and nvidia.ko hard-fails ENODEV instead of
    # register-and-wait if the GPU isn't present at insmod time. Tried and reverted:
    # machine.kernel.modules (infinite ENODEV retry loop with dock disconnected;
    # hard node hang minutes after a successful load when nvidia_drm was included,
    # suspected i915 conflict; retry loop alone destabilized the node even without
    # nvidia_drm). Even with machine.kernel.modules removed, simply having the
    # extensions installed left `ext-nvidia-persistenced`/`ext-nvidia-cdi-gen`
    # polling indefinitely in the "waiting for services" boot task - confirmed via
    # dmesg to have caused two more unattended hard resets that same night (21:04 and
    # 22:15 EDT), both caught by Talos's own hardware watchdog (iTCO_wdt, 5m timeout)
    # after the runtime hung. Filed as siderolabs/talos discussion #13896; a
    # maintainer also confirmed the DRA driver is documented to require GPU Operator
    # underneath (devicePlugin.enabled=false), not standalone as this repo assumed -
    # see CLAUDE.md. 2026-07-28: reverted to true baseline (schematic has zero NVIDIA
    # extensions, same as k8s-0/k8s-1) - not safe to run the eGPU schematic unattended
    # even without machine.kernel.modules. Next attempt needs machine.udev.rules
    # triggering modprobe only on the actual PCI hotplug "add" event for vendor
    # 0x10de, and/or GPU Operator installed underneath DRA - neither done yet.
    # 2026-07-29: confirmed the dock exposes a USB Realtek NIC (driver r8152) -
    # blacklisted via schematic.yaml.j2, applied to k8s-2 only for now (harmless
    # on k8s-0/k8s-1 too, just not urgent to reconcile their image today).
    # Deliberately NOT combined with another NVIDIA extensions/modules attempt -
    # that failure mode is unrelated to networking and already reproduced twice;
    # keeping this an isolated, single-variable change.
    image: factory.talos.dev/installer/46f6e58143bcb9c64c9460947ffb7536357d48c496fe05940bf6c8fca69d61e7:v1.13.7 # baseline, no NVIDIA extensions, net.ifnames=0 removed, r8152 blacklisted - see `just talos gen-schematic-id`
    wipe: false
---
apiVersion: v1alpha1
kind: HostnameConfig
hostname: k8s-2
